'''Pagetti Rook''' was a [[Weequay]] [[Gender|male]] who worked for the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] as a [[skiff]] guard on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. In [[4 ABY]], Jabba ordered that [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]]&mdash;three agents of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] whom he held prisoner&mdash;be [[Death|executed]] at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]]. Rook was assigned to the [[Bantha-II cargo skiff]] that carried the prisoners to the pit, where they were to be fed to a [[sarlacc]] that lived there.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Move him into position.|translated=1|Jabba orders Rook to push Luke Skywalker to the end of the skiff's gangplank|<ref name="ROTJ" />}}
Pagetti Rook<ref name="Force Collection">''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]''</ref> was a [[Weequay]] who served the [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] as a [[skiff]] [[Skiff guard|guard]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="DB" /> During his time in Jabba's service as a skiff guard, Rook escorted the [[gangster]]'s former substitute [[majordomo]] to be fed to the [[sarlacc]], a creature used as a method of [[Death|execution]] by the Hutt.<ref name="SWA">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=23|story=Tales from Wild Space: Majordomo, Major Problems}}</ref>

[[File:Skiff_ST.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Rook rode on board a skiff to the Great Pit of Carkoon.]]
In [[8 BBY|8]] or [[7 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{KenobiComicsDate}}</ref> alongside a [[Klatooinian]] guard, Rook was assigned by his master to follow the [[Wookiee]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Krrsantan]] to the [[Dune Sea]] to track down the man that stopped his [[water tax]] during the [[Great Drought]]. They went to the [[Lars homestead|Lars moisture farm]] and took [[Owen Lars]] hostage. However, the attempt ended in failure as the [[Exile (punishment)|exiled]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], the one responsible for stopping Jabba's water tax, came to fight the Wookiee, and both he and Lars defeated him, prompting Krrsantan to leave Tatooine to avoid Jabba's wrath.<ref name="SW20:FtJoOBK">[[Star Wars (2015) 20|''Star Wars'' (2015) 20]]</ref>

His master obtained the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] frozen in [[carbonite]]<ref name="ROTJ" /> in [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> and displayed Solo at [[Boba Fett's Palace|his palace]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]], where Rook worked.<ref name="ROTJ" /> In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> several of Solo's friends in the Alliance initiated a [[Rescue of Han Solo|plan to free the smuggler]] from Jabba's clutches, which started with the former smuggler [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] taking a job alongside Rook as a skiff guard at the palace. The [[Jedi Knight]] [[Luke Skywalker]] then gifted the [[droid]]s [[R2-D2]] and [[C-3PO]] to Jabba, and they both were given roles within the palace. With these allies in place, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] disguised herself as the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boushh]] and brought Chewbacca to Jabba as a prisoner, but soon after arriving she was caught thawing Solo out of his carbonite and captured. Skywalker was the last to journey to the palace, and after he killed Jabba's pet [[rancor]], the Hutt ordered that Solo, Chewbacca and Skywalker be executed.<ref name="ROTJ" />

[[File:BD1cutter.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Pagetti Rook wields his vibro-ax]]
Rook was one of five guards assigned to escort the prisoners<ref name="ROTJ" /> on a [[Bantha-II cargo skiff]]<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> [[pilot]]ed by the [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] [[Vedain]],<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> with Calrissian,<ref name="ROTJ" /> fellow Weequay [[Rintel Aren]],<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Battle of Hoth and the Second Death Star}}</ref>, the [[human]] [[Velken Tezeri]]<ref name="AEYNTK" /> and the [[Slavery|slave]] [[Kithaba]]<ref name="CEUE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> also assigned to the skiff. The skiff took Skywalker and his companions to the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]], where they were to be fed to the sarlacc that dwelt there and digested over one thousand years. Jabba and his court traveled in the [[sail barge]]<ref name="ROTJ" /> ''[[Khetanna]]''<ref name="USW" /> to watch the spectacle, and a second skiff of guards traveled alongside the vehicle carrying Rook.<ref name="ROTJ" /> Upon reaching the pit, Skywalker used a Jedi [[mind trick]] to convince one of his guards to take off his [[Stuncuffs|handcuffs]]<ref name="Beware" /> before Rook forced him out onto a gangplank over the sarlacc's pit. Jabba offered the prisoners a chance to beg for mercy, but all three refused, and Skywalker warned the Hutt that this was his last chance to free them. Jabba ignored the threat and ordered Rook to push Skywalker into the pit.<ref name="ROTJ" />

Rook stepped forward and jabbed at the Jedi with his<ref name="ROTJ" /> [[BD-1 Cutter vibro-ax]],<ref name="CT">{{SWCT|set=The Armory|cardname=BD-1 Cutter Vibro-ax}}</ref> forcing Skywalker to step off the end of the plank; however, the Jedi spun, caught the plank, and leapt back up and over Rook. After landing, Skywalker caught [[Luke Skywalker's green lightsaber|his lightsaber]], which had been launched to him by R2-D2 on board the sail barge, and attacked Rook and his colleagues. At some point during the ensuing battle, Rook was killed.<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Personality and traits==
Pagetti Rook was a Weequay<ref name="DB" /> [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Beware" /> with [[Color|black]] [[hair]] and brown skin.<ref name="ROTJ" />

Rook was able to speak [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="SW20:FtJoOBK" /> He could also understand [[Huttese]], as demonstrated during his tenure as Jabba Desilijic Tiure's guard.<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Equipment==
Rook carried a BD-1 Cutter [[vibro-ax]]<ref name="USW" /> while on the skiff and wore a pair of beige pants with a blue shirt and brown [[armor]]. His outfit also included [[boot]]s and a [[belt]].<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Behind the scenes==
Pagetti Rook was one of several Weequay characters created for the [[1983]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']],<ref name="ROTJ" /> all of whom were known as "Queequay" by the crew of ''Return of the Jedi''<ref name="I67">{{InsiderCite|67|Set Piece|Set Piece: Jabba's Sail Barge}}</ref> during production<ref name="Costume">''[[Star Wars Costumes: The Original Trilogy]]''</ref> in reference to the fictional [[Wikipedia:Polynesia|Polynesian]] harpooner [[Wikipedia:Queequeg|Queequeg]] from [[Wikipedia:Herman Melville|Herman Melville's]] 1851 novel [[Wikipedia:Moby-Dick|''Moby-Dick'']]. The Weequay species were named after Queequeg.<ref name="Databank">{{DB|species|weequay|Weequay}}</ref> Rook himself, who was portrayed by stuntman [[Peter Diamond]]<ref name="Actor">{{Blogspot|subdomain=starwarsaficionado|url=2014/09/behind-scenes-just-another-day-at-skiff.html|name=STAR WARS AFICIONADO|text=Behind the Scenes: Just Another Day at the Skiff!}}</ref> and known as "Queequeg 2" in production,<ref name="Costume" /> was identified by the nickname "Queequeg" in ''[[Star Wars: The Action Figure Archive]]'', a reference book released in [[1999]].<ref name="AFA">''[[Star Wars: The Action Figure Archive]]''</ref> The character received proper identification in the [[Rogues Gallery (department)|''Rogues Gallery'']] section of ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' [[Star Wars Insider 143|143]], where [[Lucasfilm Story Group]]'s [[Leland Chee]] identified him by the full name of Pagetti Rook.<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|143|Rogues Gallery|Rogues Gallery: Jabba's Henchmen!}}</ref> With the first letters swapped, Rintel Aren and Pagetti Rook [[Tuckerization|share their first names]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> with [[W:c:pirates:Pintel and Ragetti|Pintel and Ragetti]], a pirate duo from the ''[[Wikipedia:Pirates of the Caribbean (film series)|Pirates of the Caribbean]]'' franchise. The last names are based on the last names of their actors, [[W:c:pirates:Lee Arenberg|Lee Arenberg]] and [[W:c:pirates:Mackenzie Crook|Mackenzie Crook]].<ref name="POTC">''[[Wikipedia:Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl|Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl]]''</ref>

All of the non-human skiff guard costumes, including Rook's, were made through cooperation between the costume and creature design departments working on the film. Clay sculpts of the alien heads were used to make plaster molds into which latex could be poured to create the final product. Velcro and harnesses hidden with clothing were used to make sure the masks did not fall off the performers' heads during filming. Rook's clothing consisted of a quilted suede tabard over a simple turquoise shirt. The pants were made using a cotton waffle weave fabric that was used extensively in many of the film's costumes and then dyed, aged and distressed with mud. The leather straps and belt that lay over the tabard were secured at the front of the costume with a medallion buckle. An early costume sketch for the character made by [[Nilo Rodis-Jamero]] also included a helmet and armed the Weequay with a [[blaster]] as well as a vibro-ax.<ref name="Costume" />

